                <pb facs="0700" n="598" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg598"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/710c: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-02-27T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 27,
                                1919, 6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Impress upon the Chinese Government importance of formal approval of the plan for
                    operation of Siberian railways and prompt designation of representatives on
                    commission. The plan as submitted has now been formally approved by Great
                    Britain and France as well as by the United States and Japan and consequently
                    has gone too far for any modification of principle.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
